---
import LegalServiceLayout from '../../components/LegalServiceLayout.astro';
const adoptionTypes = [
  { title: 'Stepparent Adoptions', description: 'Establish legal parentage for a spouse of an existing legal parent, after addressing any required termination or other eligibility conditions.' },
  { title: 'Relative Adoptions', description: 'Help a relative pursue permanent legal parentage through the applicable Wisconsin court process.' },
  { title: 'Confirmatory LGBTQ+ Adoptions', description: 'Evaluate an adoption order to confirm and secure intended legal parentage for LGBTQ+ families, based on existing parentage, marital status, and statutory eligibility.' },
];
---
<LegalServiceLayout title="Wisconsin TPR & Adoption Attorney" description="Virtual Wisconsin legal counsel for voluntary and involuntary termination of parental rights, stepparent and relative adoption, and confirmatory LGBTQ+ adoption." canonicalPath="/legal-services/tpr-adoption" breadcrumbLabel="TPR & Adoption" headline="Building and Securing Families: TPR & Adoption" subheadline="Professional, virtual legal counsel to navigate Wisconsin’s adoption and termination processes with compassion and care." ctaHeading="Take the next step toward securing your family.">
  <section class="container-shell py-16 sm:py-24" aria-labelledby="tpr-title"><div class="grid gap-7 lg:grid-cols-[auto_1fr]"><span class="eyebrow inline-flex h-14 items-center border border-gold px-5 text-forest">Step 1</span><div class="min-w-0"><h2 id="tpr-title" class="max-w-4xl text-3xl leading-tight text-forest sm:text-4xl">Voluntary &amp; Involuntary Termination of Parental Rights (TPR)</h2><p class="mt-7 max-w-4xl text-lg leading-9 text-onyx/80">Where legally required, a TPR proceeding addresses existing parental rights before an adoption can establish a new legal bond. The appropriate path depends on the child’s existing legal parentage and the proposed adoption.</p><div class="mt-9 grid gap-6 lg:grid-cols-2"><article class="border border-forest/20 bg-white p-7"><h3 class="text-2xl text-forest">Voluntary TPR</h3><p class="mt-5 text-base leading-8 text-onyx/80">A parent’s informed consent is presented through the required court process. Consent by itself does not complete a termination; the court must make the necessary findings and enter an order.</p></article><article class="border border-forest/20 bg-white p-7"><h3 class="text-2xl text-forest">Involuntary TPR</h3><p class="mt-5 text-base leading-8 text-onyx/80">A contested proceeding requires proof of a statutory ground and a court decision addressing the child’s best interests. Careful preparation and compliance with procedural protections are essential.</p></article></div></div></div></section>
  <section class="border-y border-gold/30 bg-forest-dark py-16 text-parchment sm:py-24" aria-labelledby="adoption-title"><div class="container-shell"><div class="grid gap-7 lg:grid-cols-[auto_1fr]"><span class="eyebrow inline-flex h-14 items-center border border-gold px-5 text-gold-light">Step 2</span><div class="min-w-0"><h2 id="adoption-title" class="max-w-4xl text-3xl leading-tight sm:text-4xl">Stepparent, Relative, and Confirmatory LGBTQ+ Adoptions</h2><p class="mt-7 max-w-4xl text-lg leading-9 text-parchment/85">An adoption order establishes permanent legal parentage. Counsel helps identify the appropriate petition, supporting information, and court process for your family’s circumstances.</p><div class="mt-9 grid gap-6 xl:grid-cols-3">{adoptionTypes.map((type) => <article class="border border-gold/30 bg-forest p-7"><h3 class="text-2xl leading-snug text-gold-light">{type.title}</h3><p class="mt-5 text-base leading-8 text-parchment/80">{type.description}</p></article>)}</div><p class="mt-8 max-w-4xl border-l-2 border-gold pl-5 text-base leading-8 text-parchment/80">These steps are a planning framework, not a requirement that every adoption begin with TPR. In a qualifying stepparent adoption, the existing spouse-parent’s rights are preserved. Confirmatory adoption needs are evaluated individually.</p></div></div></div></section>
</LegalServiceLayout>
